{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Types of Programming Languages", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when talking about types of programming languages.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Talk about principles, concepts, and characteristics of general-purpose computer programming language in spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Exchanges simple information on principles, concepts, and features of general purpose computer programming languages.  Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Future With the Present Continuous", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>Typically, you use the <strong>present continuous</strong> to talk about actions that are happening at the moment of speaking. Another common use of the <strong>present continuous</strong> is to talk about <strong>future arrangements</strong>.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p>You can use the <strong>present continuous</strong> to talk about <strong>arrangements</strong> in the <strong>future</strong> that you have already planned.</p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i>I<strong>&rsquo;m meeting </strong>the team of developers next week.</i></p> <p>It is recommended to mention a <strong>time expression</strong> that refers to the <strong>future</strong> to make it clear that you are talking about a <strong>future</strong> <strong>event</strong> instead of an action that is happening now.</p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i>She <strong>is taking</strong> a training course on high-level languages <strong>next month</strong>.</i></p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "He is talking about the types of programming languages. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What is Mr. Douglas explaining today?", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Compilers and Interpreters", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>When you talk about high-level languages, you need to know what <strong>compilers</strong> and <strong>interpreters</strong> are.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p><strong>Compilers</strong> and <strong>interpreters</strong> are the two ways programmers use to translate high-level languages into machine codes; it means the ways computer can understand the program. <strong>Compilers</strong> and <strong>interpreters</strong> are different systems that provide different advantages:</p> <p><strong>Compilers</strong></p> <p>A compiler is a program that translates the source code or high-level language into machine code all at once. This means that the translation is only done once, and it has to be done before we can execute the program in order to obtain an output.</p> <p><strong>Interpreter</strong></p> <p>An interpreter also translates high-level language into machine code, but it does it differently. It translates the code at the same time the program is executed, so every time you execute the program, the code translation in happening simultaneously.</p> <p>Each system has its advantages. Let's see:</p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Compiler\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Interpreter\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>It is faster.</li><li>It doesn't reveal the source code.</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>It is more flexible and interactive.</li><li>It is translated as needed. </li></ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "interpreter  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a computer program that translates high-level code into machine code at the moment of running it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: An interpreter will translate the code line during the execution.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "English-like ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "similar to the English language", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Assembly language, which uses English-like instructions, makes machine code more readable by programmers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "run", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to execute a program or code ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You ought to compile the code first before running it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "portable ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "able to be carried or stored in a flash drive easily ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You might want to use a high-level language code to run it on different hardware because it is portable.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "translate ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to convert data, information, or codes into a different codi